From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Trall9 <tralllll9@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:21:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/18] be7000: schedutil governor, log-dump/ram-guard fixes,
 USB PHY reset

- cpu_perf: schedutil instead of performance (22.10 A/B: same Wi-Fi/WAN
  throughput, CPU-bound load ramps to 1488 MHz instantly, idle 936 MHz,
  -1 C); drops the old performance line from a kept rc.local.
- wifi-check: expect schedutil.
- log-dump: join the ring by the last written line instead of the first;
  with a full 2 MB ring the first line changed every tick and every run
  appended a full dump (rotation every ~45 min, history lost).
- ram-guard: top-3 by RSS+swap from /proc (ps w prints large VSZ as
  "108m", which broke the sort).
- usb-watchdog: full dwc3 + USB PHY reset once when the disk does not come
  back after a cold boot (17.10); usb-hangwatch init and 05-usb-disk-guard
  hotplug (08.10).
- health-check: services with autostart disabled are INFO, not WARN.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
